<title>BELGIUM: Spector 1996 profit falls, holds dividend.</title>
<headline>Spector 1996 profit falls, holds dividend.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Twelve months to December 31, 1996 (in millions of Belgian francs unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net per share (francs) *     22.5  vs  71.1</p>
<p>    Gross dividend (francs)*     33.3  vs  33.3</p>
<p>    Group net profit		  108  vs   235</p>
<p>NOTE - Spector is a Belgian photo processing group. * number of outstanding shares rose 45 percent to 4,796,925 in 1996 as result of capital increase linked to acquisitions.  </p>
<p>    Turnover			 15,540  vs 8,053</p>
<p>    Operating profit		  775  vs   607</p>
<p>    Current profit		    326  vs   391</p>
<p>    Exceptional profit		 20  vs     7 loss</p>
<p>    Pretax profit		     178  vs   297</p>
<p>    Cash flow			 1,584  vs 1,214</p>
<p>NOTE - In a statement, Spector said current earnings were influenced negatively by the setting aside of a 223 million Belgian franc provision on loans made to  Interdiscount France.</p>
<p>It also noted that a change in accounting practice had a positive impact equivalent to 69 million francs on 1996 results, which were also influenced by the change in consolidation linked to acquisitions.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
</text>
